Up to now, major efforts have on diluted magneticors (MS) in which the hosticonducting matrix is randomly substituted by transition metal () ions such as Mn, Cr, Ni, Fe or Co \cite{Diet02}. In 2002, carrier mediated ferromagnetism was reported in  MBE grown Ge{.94}$0}$ films by Park \et al.} The maximum critical temperature was 116 K. Recently many publications indicate a significant increase of $T_{C}$ in Ge{1-x}$$_}$ material depending on growth conditions{Pint05,Li05,tsui03}. Taking into account the strong tendency of Mn ions to form interlic compounds in germanium, a detailed investigation of the nanoscale structure is required. Up to now, only a few studies have focused on the nanoscale composition in Ge$_{1-x}$$_x}$ films. \cite{Kang05} who evidenced a micrometer scale segregation of manganese in large Mn rich stripes. Ge$_3$n$_5$ as well as Ge$_8$n$_{11}$ clusters embedded in a germanium matrix have been reported by many authors. Ge$_3$n$_5$ clusters exhibit aie temperature of 296 Kcite{Mass90}. This phase frequently observed in Ge$_{1-x}$$_}$ films is the most stable (Gen) alloy. The other stable compound Ge$_8$n$_{1}$ has also been observed in nanocrallites surrounded with pure germanium{Park01}. Ge$_$}$ and$_$_5$ phases are ferromagnetic but their metallic character considerablyates their potential use as spin injectors.
Recently, some new Mn-rich nanostructures have been evidenced in Ge$_{1-x}$$_{x}$ layers.cite{Sugh05} reported the of high Mn content (between 10 \% 20 \% of Mn)ous Ge$_{1-x}$$_x$ precipitates  in a Mn-free germanium matrix. Mn-rich coherent cubic clusters were observed by Ahlers \textitet al.}{Ahle06} which exhibit aie temperatures below 200 K. Finally, high-$T_{}$ ($>$ 400 K) Mn-rich nanocolumns have been evidenced{Jame06} which could lead to silicon compatible room temperature operational devices.\\
In the present paper, we investigate the structural and magnetic properties of Ge$_1-x}$$_x$ thin films for low growth temperatures ($<$ 20$^{\circ}$C) and low Mn concentrations (between 1 \% and 11 \%). We show that depending on growth conditions, we obtain either Mn-rich nanolumns or Ge$_{3}$Mn$_{5}$ clusters embedded in aium matrix. We discuss the structural and magnetic properties of these nanostructures as a of manganese concentration and growth temperature. We also discuss the magneticisropy of nanolumns and  
Ge$_3$n$_5$ clusters. 

