{\bf The proportion of classes}: The total number of objects is 74,515.bf The distribution of instance sizes}: Figure \{sum}() shows an instance size distribution ofO. \ph{Percent of image size} represents the ratio of object area to image area, and \ph{Percent of instance} represents the ratio of the corresponding number of objects to the total number of objects.bf The instance number per image}: Figure \ref{sum}(b) illustrates the number of categories per image forO. \ph{Number of instances} represents the of objects one image has, and \{ Percentage of images} represents the ratio of the corresponding number of images to of images. Most images contain between 5 and 15 instances, with an average of 9.57 instances image.

For PASCAL VOC \cite{Everingham2007The} or COCO{ie2014}, roughly 50\% of all objects occupy no than 10\% of the image itself, and others evenly occupy from 10\% to 10\%. 
In the aspect of instances number per image, COCO contains 7.7 instances per image and VOC contains 3. In comparison,O has .57 instances per image and most instances less than 1.5\% of the image size.
,O contains almost exclusively massive small instances and has the long-tail distribution at the same time, which means it is promising to design a detector to with massive small objects and stay high efficiency at the time for underwater robot picking.

