In, in a wide of growth temperatures and Mn concentrations, we have evidenced a two-dimensional spinodal decomposition to the of Mn-rich nans in Ge$_1}$M$_x}$ films. This decomposition is probably the of: $()$ a strong pair between Mn atoms,)$ a strong surface diffusion of Mn atoms inium even at low growth temperatures and)$ layer layer growth conditions. We have also investigated the of growth parameters on the decomposition: at low growth temperatures (100$^circC), increasing the Mn content to higher columns densities while at higher temperatures (10C), the columns density remains nearly constant whereas their size increases drastically. By plotting the nanolumns density a of Mn content, we have shown that the mechanism of Mn incorporation in Ge changes above 5 \% Mn. \{agnetic properties \{magnetic}}

